Technical
### Changed

- Integrate the M9 frontend redesign branches into `main` and include the v1.9.0 release notes, bringing the milestone together at one release point. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- Add citation badges anchored in sanitized assistant Markdown, number them consistently with the sources list, and retain unanchored citations in that list. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- Add actionable suggested ticket steps as primary controls in the ticket header, with remaining suggestions in an overflow menu and existing generic actions available as fallback. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- Add a keyboard-operable command palette available across pages, with navigation entries from `NavRegistry` and debounced, cancellable ticket search. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- Add optimistic status updates to the board and ticket detail view, reconciling successful changes and restoring prior state when a change is rejected. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- Replace ticket status and assignee dialogs with inline `MudMenu` popovers that apply changes without navigating away from the ticket. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- Add inline citation badges with hover and keyboard-focus previews to assistant answers, retaining a numbered sources list for citations that are not anchored in the answer. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- Add the active agent roster to each chat system prompt so the assistant can name valid agents without first making a failed `assign_ticket` call. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- Require `AgentLoop` to run `check_grounding` once after retrieval when a grounding check has not already run, before streaming the answer. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- Add shared design tokens for colors, spacing, radius, elevation, and semantic chip colors, and replace `KpiCard.Accent` color strings with the `KpiAccent` tone enum. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- Fix board card title wrapping so long titles clamp to two lines with an ellipsis instead of expanding the card without bound. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- Fix the assistant chat panel styling so the composer and send button stay inset within the panel and aligned at narrow widths. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- Fix the ticket queue `Category` column width and header styling to prevent overlap with `Due` and align the header with its cells. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- Add system-prompt rules that prevent the assistant from claiming a write succeeded without a successful tool result and avoid needless confirmation when a requested change is clear. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- Convert ticket summary timestamps to the configured `Anthropic:UserTimeZone` before including them in the model prompt. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- Report technical failures from `search_knowledge_base` as errors while keeping the unavailable path distinct and non-error. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- Add semantic grounding evaluation using embedding similarity, with the lexical evaluator retained as a fallback when embeddings are unavailable or fail. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))

